      en: "Paro Rice Terraces are iconic agricultural landscapes in the Paro Valley. These terraced fields have been cultivated for centuries using traditional irrigation channels. The primary variety grown is Paro red rice, known for its nutty flavor and nutritional value. The terraces turn vibrant green during the monsoon and golden during harvest. They provide picturesque views and are popular among hikers. Rice farming supports the local economy and is integral to Bhutan's cultural heritage.",
