      en: "Haa Valley Yak Pastures are located in western Bhutan at elevations above 3,500 m. Yak herding is a traditional livelihood for local pastoralists. The pastures cover extensive alpine meadows. Yaks provide milk, meat, and wool for the herders. During summer, herders move to higher pastures. The Haa Valley is known for its pristine landscapes. The best time to visit is June to September. Herders live in simple tents while tending their herds.",
